WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:12.562
Hi, I am Mario Morales, from the University of Arizona. This is our APHA 2026 poster. We used AI agents under our own written rules, and we checked their work against the original manuals.

2
00:00:13.662 --> 00:00:18.510
About one in four adolescents in the English-speaking Caribbean has a mental-health problem.

3
00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:25.280
A review of 50 trials in 19 low- and middle-income countries found that life-skills programs help.

4
00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:33.082
And in 2025, a Hillside Health Care survey at Toledo Community College found a need for each of our seven planned modules.

5
00:00:34.182 --> 00:00:47.718
Good manuals are free online, but some run to 500 pages, too many for our small team to read. So we asked whether AI agents could help researchers find, read, and choose activities for one school in the Toledo District.

6
00:00:48.368 --> 00:00:54.872
We did this in January and February 2026, when this kind of work was still new for a project like ours.

7
00:00:55.972 --> 00:01:00.700
I designed the AI workflow, wrote its rules, and set the inclusion criteria.

8
00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:06.054
Aimee checked random samples against the manuals and advised on cultural adaptation.

9
00:01:06.704 --> 00:01:11.456
Gabriela, our co-principal investigator, provided institutional support.

10
00:01:12.106 --> 00:01:20.554
The agents had three roles. One extracted, one checked against the PDF, and one flagged problems with culture, safety, or cost.

11
00:01:21.654 --> 00:01:26.142
An AI agent ran 27 web searches and found 60 records.

12
00:01:26.792 --> 00:01:32.504
The agents read 38 manuals in full, 5,074 pages in all.

13
00:01:33.154 --> 00:01:38.794
They catalogued more than 1,100 activities, each with a quote and a page number.

14
00:01:39.444 --> 00:01:42.972
And we chose 95 of them for the THRIVE-Belize manual.

15
00:01:44.072 --> 00:01:49.832
First, the agent found free manuals for grades 6 to 12 with real classroom activities.

16
00:01:50.482 --> 00:01:59.122
Second, following my rules, the agents read each PDF in 10-page pieces and recorded every activity in 17 fields.

17
00:01:59.772 --> 00:02:05.700
Third, Aimee compared a random 20 percent of the activities in the first manuals with the originals.

18
00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:11.990
Fourth, the agents ranked activities by fit, and Aimee and I approved each module.

19
00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:15.082
The result is seven modules.

20
00:02:15.732 --> 00:02:17.676
Communication and emotions.

21
00:02:18.326 --> 00:02:20.246
Gender norms and boys' health.

22
00:02:20.896 --> 00:02:23.008
Sexual and reproductive health.

23
00:02:23.658 --> 00:02:25.530
Healthy relationships.

24
00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:28.052
Mental and physical health.

25
00:02:28.702 --> 00:02:30.694
Substance use and refusal.

26
00:02:31.344 --> 00:02:33.216
And environment and climate.

27
00:02:33.866 --> 00:02:37.850
That makes 31 sessions of 40 minutes, all on paper.

28
00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:46.678
We adapted activities for Toledo and logged every change. A generic food chain became sardine, snapper, and barracuda.

29
00:02:47.328 --> 00:02:51.288
Students now design warning labels in six local languages.

30
00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:56.594
And video scenarios became read-aloud scenarios, so no projector is needed.

31
00:02:57.694 --> 00:03:04.534
And the agents followed rules they could not override, from the right to pass to a quote and a page for every activity.

32
00:03:05.634 --> 00:03:14.850
We completed Phase 1 in July and August 2026, with feedback from students, teachers, parents, school leaders, and community members.

33
00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:26.750
The take-home. With clear criteria and careful checks, AI agents let a small team read thousands of pages and build a curriculum in which every activity traces to its source.

34
00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:35.392
Aimee's spot checks found skipped or partly invented activities, so we required complete extraction, with three counts that must match.

35
00:03:36.492 --> 00:03:41.892
Thank you. The poster, this video, and our abstract are in the repository shown here.
